What to learn for each module

For every module, try to understand:

Purpose – What AWS service does it manage?
Inputs (variables) – What configuration can you provide?
Outputs – What values does it expose for other modules?
Dependencies – Which modules or resources does it rely on?
Common options – Which settings are most frequently customized?
For every module, try to understand:

Purpose – What AWS service does it manage?
Inputs (variables) – What configuration can you provide?
Outputs – What values does it expose for other modules?
Dependencies – Which modules or resources does it rely on?
Common options – Which settings are most frequently customized?

For example, with the EC2 module:

Inputs: instance_type, ami, subnet_id, vpc_security_group_ids
Outputs: id, arn, private_ip, public_ip
Dependencies: VPC, subnet, security group, IAM role (optional)




